{
  "_comment": [
    "Listen & Learn's curated on-air QSO vocabulary (#182), pinned for both",
    "ports: MorseData.qsoElements in ios/Sources/MorseKit/MorseDataQSO.swift and",
    "android/.../morsekit/MorseDataQSO.kt. Read by",
    "ios/Sources/MorseKitCheck/main.swift and",
    "android/app/src/test/.../morsekit/MorseDataQSOTest.kt.",
    "",
    "One ordered list of 100 items, most common first, so the Top 20 tier is",
    "the first 20 and the Top 100 tier is the whole list (the tier sizes are",
    "in `tiers`). Each item is the token as displayed plus the meaning spoken",
    "after it is spelled out. Written from operating practice (Morse Code",
    "Ninja's QSO elements, ARRL, KB6NU), not captured from either port.",
    "",
    "Token spelling: letters, digits, ? and / are sent as text; a space is a",
    "word gap; a token in angle brackets (<AR>, <K>, <KN>, <SK>, <BK>) is a",
    "prosign spelled exactly as MorseData.prosigns spells it and is sent",
    "run-together from that table's pattern. Meanings for tokens that also",
    "appear in MorseData.abbreviations, qCodes or prosigns repeat those",
    "tables' wording; the tests check they agree.",
    "",
    "Brief readback (#210): Listen & Learn can speak the token spelled out",
    "and then the meaning (the default), or the meaning alone. The brief form",
    "of a meaning is the text before its first ' — ' qualifier, trimmed; a",
    "meaning with no qualifier is its own brief form. `brief.examples` pins",
    "the rule on both ports (MorseData.briefMeaning); every meaning's brief",
    "form must be non-empty and free of ' — '."
  ],
  "brief": {
    "separator": " — ",
    "examples": [
      { "meaning": "go ahead — named station only", "brief": "go ahead" },
      { "meaning": "break — back to you", "brief": "break" },
      { "meaning": "five nine nine — with N cut for 9", "brief": "five nine nine" },
      { "meaning": "five nine nine, thank you — the contest exchange", "brief": "five nine nine, thank you" },
      { "meaning": "thanks", "brief": "thanks" },
      { "meaning": "your / you're", "brief": "your / you're" },
      { "meaning": "  padded — with a qualifier  ", "brief": "padded" }
    ]
  },
  "tiers": {
